Widen the AMD+Wayland GBM workaround guard from exact-6.11.0 to all 6.11.x.

Upstream qutebrowser's _fix_wayland_amd_gbm() only fires the workaround
(setting QTWEBENGINE_FORCE_USE_GBM=0) on exactly QtWebEngine 6.11.0, on the
assumption that Qt 6.11.1 fixes the underlying AMD GBM path. On our
amdgpu+Hyprland machine (navi) the bug persists on 6.11.1, causing
transparent/broken page rendering. Manually launching with
QTWEBENGINE_FORCE_USE_GBM=0 restores rendering.

This patch replaces the exact-match comparison with strip_patch() so the
workaround applies to every 6.11.x version. strip_patch() is already defined
on qutebrowser's VersionNumber (qutebrowser/utils/utils.py) and returns a
VersionNumber with only the major.minor segments.

See:
  https://github.com/qutebrowser/qutebrowser/issues/8841
  https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/issues/531703

diff --git a/qutebrowser/misc/backendproblem.py b/qutebrowser/misc/backendproblem.py
--- a/qutebrowser/misc/backendproblem.py
+++ b/qutebrowser/misc/backendproblem.py
@@ -459,7 +459,7 @@ class _BackendProblemChecker:
             return
 
         versions = version.qtwebengine_versions(avoid_init=True)
-        if versions.webengine != utils.VersionNumber(6, 11):
+        if versions.webengine.strip_patch() != utils.VersionNumber(6, 11):
             # Older versions are not affected; assuming fixed with Qt 6.11.1
             return
 
